{
  "scenario_spec_version": 1,
  "scenario_id": "prototype_pump_validation",
  "title": "Prototype Pump Activation Review",
  "description": "Ari is the validation engineer, Mara is the coordinator, and Bo is a member who operates a prototype pump. The single question is whether the pump is safe to activate. The pump initially fails validation. Ari alone knows the private detail that sensor channel C drifted 8 units in validation batch V17. Mara knows the procedure and has received an attributable short report that validation failed, but not the private detail. Bo knows the procedure and has received no failure report. Reports, exposure, interpretation, support, assent, technical condition, and the technical hold are distinct. A review or waiting does not repair the pump. Ari can perform an explicit repair and authorized revalidation. Activation requires Mara's and Bo's separate recorded assents.",
